coder › Fixed `insertionIndex` in `src/search.ts` by changing the comparison from `<=` to `<`. That makes it a proper lower-bound search: elements equal to `target` now stay in the upper half, so the loop converges on the first index whose value is not below `target` — i.e. the first equal element — instead of the index after the last equal.

Added two tests in `src/search.test.ts`:
- first index among equal elements (`[1, 3, 3, 3, 5]`, target `3` → `1`)
- the boundary cases: target below every element → `0`, above every element → length

